-- The `@export`-everything hatch, which is what `not-ok/export-chain-broken.l4`
-- refuses the absence of — and the only file in the Catala corpus that carries a
-- module-level binder at all.
--
-- Two things are exercised here that nothing else in `jl4/examples/catala/` did:
--
--   1. A section `GIVEN`. The desugarer elaborates one into a 0-ary `ASSUME` at
--      the head of its section, which `collectAssumes` picks up like any other,
--      so `the levy rate` becomes a scope `input` on every scope that reads it —
--      directly or through a call — and callers thread it through by name
--      (`output of … with { -- the_levy_rate: the_levy_rate }`).
--
--   2. A three-rung call chain in which EVERY rung is `@export`ed. That is the
--      hatch: an un-exported rung compiles to a Catala toplevel, and a scope
--      call is not legal there. The cost is one published scope per rule — the
--      author wanted `the middle` to be a private helper and cannot have one.
--
-- The emitted module is checked by `etc/validate-catala.mjs`, so this is not
-- merely a golden of what we print: `catala typecheck` and `clerk test` agree
-- that the threading is well-formed and that the numbers match L4's evaluator.

§ `Levy`
  GIVEN `the levy rate` IS A NUMBER

@export Base charge on a metered quantity, before the levy.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base` n MEANS n TIMES 2

@export The base charge with the section's levy applied.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the middle` n MEANS `the base` n TIMES (1 PLUS `the levy rate`)

@export The levied charge plus a fixed standing amount.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the top` n MEANS `the middle` n PLUS 10

-- `the base` reads no binder, so R7 can wrap it in a `#[test]` scope and the
-- emitted block carries a value L4 computed.
#EVAL `the base` 5

-- `the top` does read one, transitively, and R7 CANNOT test it: a `#[test]`
-- scope declares no inputs, so it has nowhere to get `the levy rate` from. The
-- directive is skipped with a note rather than emitted, which is why the
-- artifact below tests only the first rung. This is a real limit of R7 on
-- binder-carrying scopes, not a defect in the chain — kept here so the note is
-- visible in a golden instead of being discovered by the next reader.
#EVAL `the top` 5
